+@option{-mfxu} to the assembler.  It implies @option{-mg4mh2}.  The
+128-bit vector registers @code{wr0} to @code{wr31} hold the
+@code{vector_size (16)} types of @code{float} and 32-bit integers, which
+are 16-byte aligned.  The vector registers are preserved across calls.
+Vector arguments are passed in @code{wr0} to @code{wr31} and then on the
+stack, and vector return values in memory.  A function that keeps vector
+values on the stack aligns its frame to 16 bytes at run time.  The
+preprocessor constant @code{__V850_FXU__} is defined if this option is
+used.
+
 @opindex mrh850-abi
 @opindex mghs
 @item -mrh850-abi
